      "purpose": "Track how one piece of information moves public opinion.",
      "base_or_modification": "paper-specific",
      "summary": "Opinion of a node lies in the unit interval, with 0.5 neutral. Two nodes exchange opinion only when their difference stays below a threshold, and each moves a fraction mu toward the other. Public opinion is the mean over all nodes. On the Ebola example it settles near 0.65.",
